Import the builders from `@micacms/core`. Each builder gives plain data, so the editor can read the model from `.mica/schema.json`.

## Options of every field

| Option | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `label` | The label in the editor. Default: the key, as words. |
| `description` | Help text below the field. |
| `required` | An empty value cannot be published. Editors can save it before that. |
| `listed` | Shows the value as a column in the list of a collection. |
| `readonly` | The editor shows the value, but cannot change it. |
| `hidden` | Mica keeps the value, but the editor does not show it. |
| `group` | Fields with the same group show in one box. |
| `width` | `"full"`, `"half"` or `"third"` of the form row. |

The build stops on an option that is not in these tables, for example a typo. A field with an option from a newer `@micacms/astro` is read-only in an older Mica until you upgrade it.

## The builders

| Builder | Stores | Options |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `text()` | A string. | `minLength`, `maxLength`, `placeholder`, `default`, `pattern` (a regular expression; it must match the whole value, with the `u` flag; a group that repeats cannot contain a repeat, so `(a+)+` is refused, but `(-[0-9]+)?` is allowed), `patternMessage`. |
| `textarea()` | A string with line breaks. | `minLength`, `maxLength`, `rows`, `placeholder`, `default`. |
| `richText()` | Markdoc, in a `<key>.mdoc` file beside the entry. | `toolbar`: `"minimal"` (bold, italic, link), `"default"` (also headings and lists), `"full"` (also `strike`, `blockquote`, `horizontalRule`, `table`, `image`), or a list of these features. Also `maxLength`, `default`. |
| `number()` | A number. | `min`, `max`, `step`, `integer`, `unit` (shown in the field, for example `"m²"`), `default`. |
| `boolean()` | `true` or `false`, never empty. | `default`. |
| `date()` | `"2026-10-13"`, or with `includeTime` a date and time with its offset. | `includeTime`, `min`, `max`, `default`. |
| `email()` | An email address. | `placeholder`, `default`. |
| `url()` | A web address. | `placeholder`, `default`. |
| `slug()` | Lower-case letters, digits and hyphens. | `from`: the key of the field that gives the slug while the editor types. `maxLength`. |
| `select({ options })` | The `value` of the choice, or a list with `multiple`. | `options`: a list of `{ label, value }`. `multiple`, `default`. |
| `object({ fields })` | An object with the given fields. | `fields`, `collapsible`, `collapsed`. |
| `repeater({ fields })` | A list of objects. | `fields`, `min`, `max`, `itemLabel` (the key that names a row), `addLabel`. |
| `relation({ collection })` | The slug of an entry, or a list with `multiple`. For a reference set, the id of an item. | `collection`: a collection of the model, or a reference set. `multiple`. |
| `media()` | The path of a file, or `{ path, alt }` with `alt`. A list with `multiple`. | `accept`: `"image"` (JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP, AVIF), `"document"` (PDF), `"any"` (every type that Mica knows), or a list of `image`, `pdf`, `gpx`, `kml`, `geojson`, `zip` and `csv`. `multiple`, `max`, `alt`: `"required"` or `"optional"`. |
| `color()` | A hex colour, for example `"#0f766e"`. | `presets`: colours to choose from. `default`. |
| `coordinates()` | `{ lat, lng }`. With a map also `zoom`, from 0 to 22. | `map`: `"liberty"`, `"bright"` or `"positron"` (OpenFreeMap), or `{ style, hosts }` for a style of your own, with `https` only. The editor's browser loads the tiles from that host. |
| `tags()` | A list of short words, never null: no tags is `[]`. | `max`, `maxLength`, `suggestions`, `default`. |

## Defaults and empty values

A `default` fills the field of a new entry, and of a singleton that has no file yet. It never fills a value that is missing in a stored entry: such a value is empty, `null`, `false` or `[]`, and your templates must handle it. So a changed default does not change the stored entries, and a cleared field stays cleared.

## Values that the model does not have

A save keeps a key in `index.json` and a `.mdoc` file that the model does not declare, for example content for a field that a newer model adds. Your templates do not get them, and `npx mica check` warns about them. To delete them, see [Change the model](/docs/model-changes/). A key in a list row without `_key` is not kept, because such a row has no identity when the order changes.

## The slug of a collection

The first `slug()` among the fields of a collection is the entry's slug. It is also the name of the entry's folder, so it is never empty. A second `slug()` among the same fields stops the build. A `slug()` in an object or in a singleton is an ordinary value, for example one URL for each language.

## Where an entry is stored

Each entry is a folder `<slug>/` with `index.json`, the `.mdoc` files and the entry's media, and each singleton is a folder `<name>/` with the same files. See [Content model](/docs/content-model/).

Each rich-text field has its own `.mdoc` file, named by the field's path: `body.mdoc`, `seo.intro.mdoc`. In a `repeater()`, each row with rich text has a key, `_key`, in `index.json`, and the file names the row by its key: `sections.k3f9a2.body.mdoc`. Then a new order of the rows changes only `index.json`. Mica writes the key; do not change it. Your templates do not get it.

## Collections and singletons

```ts
import { collection, defineSite, singleton, slug, text } from "@micacms/core";

export const site = defineSite({
  root: "./content",
  collections: {
    news: collection({ label: "News", url: "/news/{slug}", fields: { title: text({ required: true }), slug: slug({ from: "title" }) } }),
  },
  singletons: {
    settings: singleton({ label: "Website", fields: { tagline: text() } }),
  },
});
```

| Option of `collection()` | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `label`, `labelSingular` | The names in the editor, for example "News" and "Article". |
| `description` | Text below the title of the list. |
| `fields` | The fields. |
| `titleField` | The key that names an entry in lists. Default: `title`, else the first `text()`, else the slug. |
| `slugField` | The key of the slug. Default: the first `slug()`. |
| `defaultSort` | `{ field, direction }` for the list in the editor. `field` is a field of the collection or `"position"`. Text sorts alphabetically in English, and a date with a time by its instant. `_mica.position` on the website follows it too: sort your pages with `inEditorOrder` from `@micacms/astro`. |
| `sortable` | Editors can put the entries in an order. Mica keeps it in `_order.json`. |
| `url` | The page of an entry on the website, with `{slug}` once, such as `/news/{slug}`. With `MICA_SITE_URL`, an entry shows "Open on website". See [Preview changes](/docs/previews/). |

`singleton()` takes `label`, `description`, `fields` and `url` (its page, such as `/about`, without `{slug}`). `defineSite()` takes `root`, `collections`, `singletons` and `references`.

## Reference sets

`referenceSet({ label, file, id, title })` declares data of the website that Mica never edits, and that a `relation()` can point to. It goes in `references` of `defineSite()`, under the name of the website's own Astro collection for that file. `file` is the file from the project root, `id` the key of an item's id (default `id`), and `title` the key that the editor shows. See [Reference data](/docs/reference-data/).
